{"step_index":65,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T13:20:51Z","thinking":"We got timeouts and OpenAI API usage error due to new API. Need to adjust code to use new openai API. Also need to adjust crawler to increase timeout or use fallback. Provide solution: migrate to openai>=1.0 usage. Implement using openai.ChatCompletion.create is deprecated; need to use openai.ChatCompletion.create? Actually new openai uses client = openai.OpenAI(). Then client.chat.completions.create(...). So modify llm.py accordingly. Also need to handle timeouts: maybe increase timeout and include retry, but we can also ignore failures and still produce output for those domains that succeeded (none succeeded because all timed out). Could use \"wait_until=load\" maybe not enough, need to increase wait and maybe use page.wait_for_load_state(\"networkidle\", timeout=30000). Also use page.goto with timeout 30000. Could also use fallback to fetch with requests for static content. For simplicity, we can adjust fetch_page to increase timeout and add try with page.wait_for_load_state \"domcontentloaded\" etc. But timeouts may be due to network restrictions? Might be blocked. Could use headless but still network should work. Possibly firewall blocking. For now, we can implement a simple HTTP GET fallback using requests to fetch page content if Playwright times out. Add that.\n\nAlso fix OpenAI usage. Let's edit llm.py to use new client.\n\nCreate new file modifications.\n\nWe'll also create a simple fallback in crawler.fetch_page: if Playwright fails, try using requests (with timeout) and return text.\n\nImplement modifications.\n\nLet's edit lead_enrichment/llm.py.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"EndLine":200,"ReplacementContent":"# lead_enrichment/llm.py\n\"\"\"LLM abstraction layer.\nImplements a simple factory that returns a concrete client based on the\nenvironment variable ``LLM_PROVIDER``.  The default implementation uses the\nOpenAI chat completion API (v1+).  The client returns a :class:`CompanyInfo`\ninstance by feeding a structured prompt and parsing the JSON response with\nPydantic.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport logging\nfrom typing import Any, Dict\n\nfrom .models import CompanyInfo\nfrom .config import load_config\n\n_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Base class\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass BaseLLM:\n    \"\"\"Abstract LLM client.\n\n    Sub‑classes must implement :meth:`extract_info` which receives the domain\n    and the cleaned markdown content and returns a :class:`CompanyInfo` model.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, config: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.config = config\n\n    async def extract_info(self, domain: str, content: str) -> CompanyInfo:  # pragma: no cover\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# OpenAI implementation (v1+ API)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass OpenAIClient(BaseLLM):\n    def __init__(self, config: Dict[str, Any]):\n        super().__init__(config)\n        try:\n            import openai\n        except ImportError as exc:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"openai package is required for OpenAIClient\") from exc\n        self.openai = openai\n        self.api_key = config.get(\"openai_api_key\")\n        if not self.api_key:\n            raise ValueError(\"OPENAI_API_KEY is not set in the environment\")\n        # Initialise the new OpenAI client (v1+)\n        self.client = self.openai.OpenAI(api_key=self.api_key)\n        self.model = config.get(\"openai_model\", \"gpt-4o-mini\")\n\n    async def extract_info(self, domain: str, content: str) -> CompanyInfo:\n        system_prompt = (\n            \"You are a lead enrichment assistant. Extract the required fields from the given\"\n            \" website content and return a JSON object that conforms exactly to the\"\n            \" following Pydantic schema:\"\n        )\n        schema = CompanyInfo.schema_json(indent=2)\n        # Truncate content to stay within token limits (approx 4k tokens ~ 12k chars)\n        truncated = content[:12000]\n        user_prompt = (\n            f\"Domain: {domain}\\n\\n\"\n            f\"Content:\\n{truncated}\\n\\n\"\n            \"Extract the information and output ONLY a JSON object matching the schema.\"\n            f\"\\nSchema:\\n{schema}\"\n        )\n        response = await self._call_chat(system_prompt, user_prompt, domain)\n        try:\n            data = json.loads(response)\n            return CompanyInfo(**data)\n        except Exception as exc:\n            _logger.exception(\"Failed to parse LLM response for %s\", domain)\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid LLM JSON response\") from exc\n\n    async def _call_chat(self, system: str, user: str, domain: str) -> str:\n        # The OpenAI python SDK v1 is synchronous; run it in a thread.\n        import asyncio\n\n        def _sync_call():\n            completion = self.client.chat.completions.create(\n                model=self.model,\n                messages=[{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user}],\n                temperature=0.0,\n            )\n            # Log token usage if available\n            usage = getattr(completion, \"usage\", None)\n            if usage:\n                from .utils import log_token_usage\n                log_token_usage(domain=domain, provider=\"openai\", prompt_tokens=usage.prompt_tokens, completion_tokens=usage.completion_tokens)\n            return completion.choices[0].message.content.strip()\n\n        return await asyncio.to_thread(_sync_call)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Factory\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef get_llm_client(config: Dict[str, Any]) -> BaseLLM:\n    provider = config.get(\"llm_provider\", \"openai\").lower()\n    if provider == \"openai\":\n        return OpenAIClient(config)\n    # Placeholder for future providers (Anthropic, Ollama, etc.)\n    raise ValueError(f\"Unsupported LLM provider: {provider}\")\n","StartLine":1,"TargetContent":"# lead_enrichment/llm.py\n\"\"\"LLM abstraction layer.\nImplements a simple factory that returns a concrete client based on the\nenvironment variable ``LLM_PROVIDER``.  The default implementation uses the\nOpenAI chat completion API (gpt-4o).  The client returns a :class:`CompanyInfo`\ninstance by feeding a structured prompt and parsing the JSON response with\nPydantic.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport logging\nfrom typing import Any, Dict\n\nfrom .models import CompanyInfo\nfrom .config import load_config\n\n_logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Base class\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass BaseLLM:\n    \"\"\"Abstract LLM client.\n\n    Sub‑classes must implement :meth:`extract_info` which receives the domain\n    and the cleaned markdown content and returns a :class:`CompanyInfo` model.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, config: Dict[str, Any]):\n        self.config = config\n\n    async def extract_info(self, domain: str, content: str) -> CompanyInfo:  # pragma: no cover\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# OpenAI implementation (v1+ API)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nclass OpenAIClient(BaseLLM):\n    def __init__(self, config: Dict[str, Any]):\n        super().__init__(config)\n        try:\n            import openai\n        except ImportError as exc:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"openai package is required for OpenAIClient\") from exc\n        self.openai = openai\n        self.api_key = config.get(\"openai_api_key\")\n        if not self.api_key:\n            raise ValueError(\"OPENAI_API_KEY is not set in the environment\")\n        # Initialise the new OpenAI client (v1+)\n        self.client = self.openai.OpenAI(api_key=self.api_key)\n        self.model = config.get(\"openai_model\", \"gpt-4o-mini\")\n\n    async def extract_info(self, domain: str, content: str) -> CompanyInfo:\n        system_prompt = (\n            \"You are a lead enrichment assistant. Extract the required fields from the given\"\n            \" website content and return a JSON object that conforms exactly to the\"\n            \" following Pydantic schema:\"\n        )\n        schema = CompanyInfo.schema_json(indent=2)\n        # Truncate content to stay within token limits (approx 4k tokens ~ 12k chars)\n        truncated = content[:12000]\n        user_prompt = (\n            f\"Domain: {domain}\\n\\n\"\n            f\"Content:\\n{truncated}\\n\\n\"\n            \"Extract the information and output ONLY a JSON object matching the schema.\"\n            f\"\\nSchema:\\n{schema}\"\n        )\n        response = await self._call_chat(system_prompt, user_prompt, domain)\n        try:\n            data = json.loads(response)\n            return CompanyInfo(**data)\n        except Exception as exc:\n            _logger.exception(\"Failed to parse LLM response for %s\", domain)\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid LLM JSON response\") from exc\n\n    async def _call_chat(self, system: str, user: str, domain: str) -> str:\n        # The OpenAI python SDK v1 is synchronous; run it in a thread.\n        import asyncio\n\n        def _sync_call():\n            completion = self.client.chat.completions.create(\n                model=self.model,\n                messages=[{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": system}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": user}],\n                temperature=0.0,\n     