{"step_index":69,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T13:21:20Z","thinking":"We need to re-run the script now that the OpenAI client updated. However we still have earlier issue: all sites timed out; the crawler didn't fetch any pages. Likely due to network restrictions or we need to increase timeout, perhaps use request.head fallback. Might be that Playwright cannot access internet due to proxy. Could try to increase timeout and not just wait for network idle. Also maybe need to ensure we use http:// scheme. In process_domain we add https if not present. That's fine.\n\nTimeouts occurred quickly (<10 secs). Could increase timeout to 30 sec. Also maybe need to disable strict TLS verification? Could also fallback to using page.goto with wait_until \"load\". Let's adjust fetch_page timeout.\n\nWe can update fetch_page in crawler to use larger timeout (e.g., 30000 ms) and increase wait_for_load_state timeout.\n\nAlso, we may consider using context.set_default_navigation_timeout. Let's modify fetch_page.\n\nAlso need to ensure we install browsers for network; they are installed.\n\nWe'll edit lead_enrichment/crawler.py accordingly.\n\nImplement:\n\n@retry_async attempts 3 with backoff 2.\n\nasync def fetch_page(page, url): set page.set_default_navigation_timeout(30000) before goto.\n\nAlso catch generic errors.\n\nWe'll replace fetch_page function.\n\nLet's edit file.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"EndLine":200,"Instruction":"Replace existing crawler implementation with increased timeouts","StartLine":1,"TargetContent":"# lead_enrichment/crawler.py\n\"\"\"Web crawling utilities using Playwright.\nThe workflow:\n1. Fetch the homepage HTML.\n2. Discover common sub‑pages (about, team, company, contact, pricing).\n3. Retrieve each page, clean it via :mod:`processor`, and concatenate the results.\nAll operations are async and include retry logic.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\nimport logging\nfrom typing import List\nfrom urllib.parse import urljoin\n\nfrom playwright.async_api import async_playwright, TimeoutError as PlaywrightTimeoutError\n\nfrom .processor import clean_html\nfrom .utils import retry_async\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nCOMMON_PATHS = [\"/about\", \"/team\", \"/company\", \"/contact\", \"/pricing\"]\n\n@retry_async(attempts=3, backoff=2)\nasync def fetch_page(page, url: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Navigate to *url* and return the page source.\n    Uses a generous timeout (30 s) and waits for the full ``load`` event.\n    Returns an empty string on failure (logged by the decorator).\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        # Increase navigation timeout for slower sites\n        page.set_default_navigation_timeout(30000)\n        await page.goto(url, wait_until=\"load\", timeout=30000)\n        # Ensure network activity has quieted down\n        await page.wait_for_load_state(\"networkidle\", timeout=10000)\n        html = await page.content()\n        return html\n    except PlaywrightTimeoutError:\n        logger.warning(\"Timeout while loading %s\", url)\n        return \"\"\n    except Exception as exc:\n        logger.exception(\"Error fetching %s: %s\", url, exc)\n        return \"\"\n\nasync def discover_subpages(base_url: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Return absolute URLs that respond successfully for common paths.\n    Uses Playwright's ``request`` API for lightweight HEAD checks.\n    \"\"\"\n    discovered = []\n    async with async_playwright() as p:\n        browser = await p.chromium.launch(headless=True)\n        context = await browser.new_context()\n        request = context.request\n        for path in COMMON_PATHS:\n            candidate = urljoin(base_url, path)\n            try:\n                resp = await request.head(candidate)\n                if resp and resp.ok:\n                    discovered.append(candidate)\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n        await context.close()\n        await browser.close()\n    return discovered\n\nasync def process_domain(domain: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Crawl *domain* and return a single cleaned markdown string.\n    Aggregates homepage and any discovered sub‑pages.\n    \"\"\"\n    base_url = f\"https://{domain}\" if not domain.startswith(\"http\") else domain\n    async with async_playwright() as p:\n        browser = await p.chromium.launch(headless=True)\n        context = await browser.new_context()\n        page = await context.new_page()\n        # 1. Homepage\n        homepage_html = await fetch_page(page, base_url)\n        contents = []\n        if homepage_html:\n            contents.append(clean_html(homepage_html))\n        # 2. Discover sub‑pages and fetch them\n        subpages = await discover_subpages(base_url)\n        for url in subpages:\n            html = await fetch_page(page, url)\n            if html:\n                contents.append(clean_html(html))\n        await context.close()\n        await browser.close()\n    return \"\\n\\n---\\n\\n\".join(filter(None, contents))\n","TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\new\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\4fdbd629-b1b9-4bee-a13c-8876484f2243\\lead_enrichment\\crawler.py"}}]}
